  "grid_title": "DIRECTIONAL TERMS",
  "why": "All from anatomical position (standing, palms forward). Proximal: in a limb, nearer the trunk or the point of attachment (the elbow is proximal to the wrist); distal: farther from it (the fingers are distal to the wrist). Medial: toward the midline; lateral: toward the side (the thumb is lateral to the other digits). Anterior (ventral): the front (the sternum is anterior to the vertebral column); posterior (dorsal): the back. Superior (cranial): higher, toward the head; inferior (caudal): lower (the pelvis is inferior to the ribs). Superficial: closer to the body's surface; deep: farther from it (the femur is deep to the thigh muscles).",
